// expect: 4
// BANKED RED (unregistered — THE SOURCE of the trial/final divergence,
// minimized 2026-07-31 from 930 wheel movers to fifteen lines). A cycle
// member's row is PUBLISHED AS A VALUE at its own decl exit — a moment
// when its co-members have not been judged — so the effects they later
// prove never reach it. Measured through the stdin judge on boot
// 74d63b7c:
//
//   self_first  trial !E1        final !E1+E2   ← LOSES the co-member's effect
//   other_b     trial !E2        final !E1+E2   ← same, mirrored
//   co_first    (no flip)                        ← accidentally correct
//   other_a     (no flip)                        ← judged second; reads a publish
//
// THE ASYMMETRY IS THE PROOF, and it inverts the obvious reading: the
// member that charges its OWN row first is the one that goes WRONG.
// Three mechanisms compose to it, each individually deliberate:
//   1. scheme_own_row charges a BARE edge (names stripped — the fix for
//      the fragment-join hazard that cost 52 Int-vs-List(Float));
//   2. tail_join keeps the FIRST var, so a second co-member's edge is
//      dropped entirely (the triple has ONE tail slot);
//   3. row_without_self CUTS a self-rooted tail to closed — freezing
//      the row at that instant and severing the surviving edge.
// When the accumulated tail happens to be a CO-MEMBER's var (co_first),
// no cut fires, the published row keeps a LIVE EDGE, and it resolves
// correctly later — the open tail is the honest form and the cut is
// what breaks it.
//
// The contract: every member of a cycle reports the WHOLE cycle's
// effects. `mentl check` on this file must show zero movers and all
// four fns carrying E1 + E2. Greens when a charge DRAWS AN EDGE into
// the callee's live row cell (N edges per cell, not one tail slot) and
// the least solution is the join's own idempotence — R ∪ R = R, no cut
// (Hβ.infer.schemes-are-edges rung 3).
effect E1 { e1() -> Int }

effect E2 { e2() -> Int }

fn self_first(n) = if n > 0 { self_first(n - 1) + other_a(n) } else { e1() }

fn other_a(n) = if n > 0 { self_first(n - 1) } else { e2() }

fn co_first(n) = if n > 0 { other_b(n) + co_first(n - 1) } else { e1() }

fn other_b(n) = if n > 0 { co_first(n - 1) } else { e2() }

fn main() = 4
